{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1523885-willpower-and-automatic-success-question","id":1523885,"title":"Willpower and automatic success question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-09T13:30:03-07:00","id":1523885,"title":"Willpower and automatic success question","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> If you have to succeed by X amount of successes (lets say 3), you roll without getting anything successes but you already spent a Willpower point, what happens?<ul><li>A) 1 Willpower point grants you 1 success but you need 2 more so you failed the task.</li> <li>B) You automatically succeed in the action (as if obtaining the 3 required successes).</li> </ul>What is the right interpretation? A, B, or a third option not mentioned here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Editing errors fixed. 10-09-2023, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T14:53:46-07:00","id":1523888,"title":"","content":"While trying to account for the fact that you didn't specify an edition or game line (and the wording on those can change subtly towards different interpretations), A is the most direct reading of the texts. Spending 1 WP grants you one additional successes (in addition to things like protecting you from botches). It does not guarantee hitting a specified number of successes for specific rules where getting less than X successes is a failure even if you have a positive number of successes.<br /> <br /> This is largely because the text of the base rules presumes have any successes left after any permutations is at least a marginal successes, not an outright failure. It's specific rules later in the texts (esp. supernatural powers) that do things like say you need X successes for a power to go off without accounting for the baseline presumption of the rule that 1 success is never supposed to be an overt failure.<br /> <br /> B is far more potent than Willpower is clearly intended to be. There are &quot;C&quot; options certain game-lines use (ex: the Threshold rules in Mage explicitly negate successes under the threshold so they become failures instead of marginal successes as Mage magic actually follows the marginal success rules for what happens if you roll less successes than you needed for the effect you wanted) to account for this if you're looking for house rules that are in-line with existing game rules to address this issue which are probably better suited to this than using B would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T15:25:01-07:00","id":1523889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1523885-willpower-and-automatic-success-question?p=1523888#post1523888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While trying to account for the fact that you didn't specify an edition or game line (and the wording on those can change subtly towards different interpretations), A is the most direct reading of the texts. Spending 1 WP grants you one additional successes (in addition to things like protecting you from botches). It does not guarantee hitting a specified number of successes for specific rules where getting less than X successes is a failure even if you have a positive number of successes.<br /> <br /> This is largely because the text of the base rules presumes have any successes left after any permutations is at least a marginal successes, not an outright failure. It's specific rules later in the texts (esp. supernatural powers) that do things like say you need X successes for a power to go off without accounting for the baseline presumption of the rule that 1 success is never supposed to be an overt failure.<br /> <br /> B is far more potent than Willpower is clearly intended to be. There are &quot;C&quot; options certain game-lines use (ex: the Threshold rules in Mage explicitly negate successes under the threshold so they become failures instead of marginal successes as Mage magic actually follows the marginal success rules for what happens if you roll less successes than you needed for the effect you wanted) to account for this if you're looking for house rules that are in-line with existing game rules to address this issue which are probably better suited to this than using B would be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> I did forgot to mention that was to be 20th edition. I was looking at the general case, but the example was the <i>Black Breath</i> power of the Path of the Four Humours in V20 as considered in<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1523854#post1523854\"> this post.</a> Essentially in that scenario, even with a Willpower expenditure is impossible to meet the target number of successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Grammar. 10-09-2023, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T16:00:16-07:00","id":1523891,"title":"","content":"V20 is one of the texts written more strongly in interpretation A's favor. When describing Automatic Successes (not bothering to roll of your dice pool is &gt;= the difficulty), it specifies that this only counts as obtaining one successes, and thus only generates marginal successes and isn't something to use in situations where that's not sufficient. It also says that spending WP is a form of Automatic Success as well, which means it should be held to the same standards of only generating that one bonus success even if it falls short.<br /> <br /> I think in that particular case of Black Breath, it's just a badly worded Resisted roll. In Resisted rolls, successes are negated, so if you roll less success than the other person, you get a failure instead of a marginal success (like if you roll less successes to dodge than they did to strike, you get hit instead of a &quot;marginal dodge&quot;); though the AoE aspect of the power kinda messes with how that works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}